            <ArticleTitle>Acute intermittent porphyria associated with hyperthyroidism.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>414-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The differential diagnosis of abdominal pain with associated hyponatraemia should include acute intermittent porphyria. Development of hyperthyroidism in a patient with latent porphyria may precipitate an acute attack and increase disease severity. Treatment of hyperthyroidism may prevent recurrent episodes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
